 from scrapling.fetchers import StealthyFetcher, StealthySession\r\n268: \r\n269: with StealthySession(headless=True, solve_cloudflare=True) as session:  # Keep the browser open until you finish\r\n270:     page = session.fetch('https://nopecha.com/demo/cloudflare', google_search=False)\r\n271:     data = page.css('#padded_content a').getall()\r\n272: \r\n273: # Or use one-off request style, it opens the browser for this request, then closes it after finishing\r\n274: page = StealthyFetcher.fetch('https://nopecha.com/demo/cloudflare')\r\n275: data = page.css('#padded_content a').getall()\r\n276: ```\r\n277: Full browser automation\r\n278: ```python\r\n279: from scrapling.fetchers import DynamicFetcher, DynamicSession\r\n280: \r\n281: with DynamicSession(headless=True, disable_resources=False, network_idle=True) as session:  # Keep the browser open until you finish\r\n282:     page = session.fetch('https://quotes.toscrape.com/', load_dom=False)\r\n283:     data = page.xpath('//span[@class=\"text\"]/text()').getall()  # XPath selector if you prefer it\r\n284: \r\n285: # Or use one-off request style, it opens the browser for this request, then closes it after finishing\r\n286: page = DynamicFetcher.fetch('https://quotes.toscrape.com/')\r\n287: data = page.css('.quote .text::text').getall()\r\n288: ```\r\n289: \r\n290: ### Spiders\r\n291: Build full crawlers with concurrent requests, multiple session types, and pause/resume:\r\n292: ```python\r\n293: from scrapling.spiders import Spider, Request, Response\r\n294: \r\n295: class QuotesSpider(Spider):\r\n296:     name = \"quotes\"\r\n297:     start_urls = [\"https://quotes.toscrape.com/\"]\r\n298:     concurrent_requests = 10\r\n299:     \r\n300:     async def parse(self, response: Response):\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
