{"step_index":51,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:54:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T22:24:26+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T22:24:26+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/find-skill-repo/all%20github%20repos/handy/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 525\nTotal Bytes: 24143\nShowing lines 1 to 150\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Handy\r\n2: \r\n3: [![Discord](https://img.shields.io/badge/Discord-%235865F2.svg?style=for-the-badge&logo=discord&logoColor=white)](https://discord.com/invite/WVBeWsNXK4)\r\n4: \r\n5: **A free, open source, and extensible speech-to-text application that works completely offline.**\r\n6: \r\n7: Handy is a cross-platform desktop application that provides simple, privacy-focused speech transcription. Press a shortcut, speak, and have your words appear in any text field. This happens on your own computer without sending any information to the cloud.\r\n8: \r\n9: ## Why Handy?\r\n10: \r\n11: Handy was created to fill the gap for a truly open source, extensible speech-to-text tool. As stated on [handy.computer](https://handy.computer):\r\n12: \r\n13: - **Free**: Accessibility tooling belongs in everyone's hands, not behind a paywall\r\n14: - **Open Source**: Together we can build further. Extend Handy for yourself and contribute to something bigger\r\n15: - **Private**: Your voice stays on your computer. Get transcriptions without sending audio to the cloud\r\n16: - **Simple**: One tool, one job. Transcribe what you say and put it into a text box\r\n17: \r\n18: Handy isn't trying to be the best speech-to-text app—it's trying to be the most forkable one.\r\n19: \r\n20: ## How It Works\r\n21: \r\n22: 1. **Press** a configurable keyboard shortcut to start/stop recording (or use push-to-talk mode)\r\n23: 2. **Speak** your words while the shortcut is active\r\n24: 3. **Release** and Handy processes your speech using Whisper\r\n25: 4. **Get** your transcribed text pasted directly into whatever a\n<truncated 4156 bytes>\nttps://github.com/cjpais/Handy/issues). We believe in transparency about the current state:\r\n117: \r\n118: ### Major Issues (Help Wanted)\r\n119: \r\n120: **Whisper Model Crashes:**\r\n121: \r\n122: - Whisper models crash on certain system configurations (Windows and Linux)\r\n123: - Does not affect all systems - issue is configuration-dependent\r\n124:   - If you experience crashes and are a developer, please help to fix and provide debug logs!\r\n125: \r\n126: **Wayland Support (Linux):**\r\n127: \r\n128: - Limited support for Wayland display server\r\n129: - Requires [`wtype`](https://github.com/atx/wtype) or [`dotool`](https://sr.ht/~geb/dotool/) for text input to work correctly (see [Linux Notes](#linux-notes) below for installation)\r\n130: \r\n131: ### Linux Notes\r\n132: \r\n133: **Text Input Tools:**\r\n134: \r\n135: For reliable text input on Linux, install the appropriate tool for your display server:\r\n136: \r\n137: | Display Server | Recommended Tool | Install Command                                    |\r\n138: | -------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\r\n139: | X11            | `xdotool`        | `sudo apt install xdotool`                         |\r\n140: | Wayland        | `wtype`          | `sudo apt install wtype`                           |\r\n141: | Both           | `dotool`         | `sudo apt install dotool` (requires `input` group) |\r\n142: \r\n143: - **X11**: Install `xdotool` for both direct typing and clipboard paste shortcuts\r\n144: - **Wayland**: Install `wtype` (preferred) or `dotool` for text input to work correctly\r\n145: - **dotool setup**: Requires adding your user to the `input` group: `sudo usermod -aG input $USER` (then log out and back in)\r\n146: \r\n147: Without these tools, Handy falls back to enigo which may have limited compatibility, especially on Wayland.\r\n148: \r\n149: **Other Notes:**\r\n150: \r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
